\par }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Music is perishable. This statement is not refuted by the amount of music that has survived for centuries and, for all we know, will \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
continue to survive. Music which we regard as immortal is an infinitesimal part of what has been submitted by composers in the last 500 years. The bulk has disappeared, and the bulk will continue to disappear, in view of the erratic rarity of genius and t
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 h\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
e vast supply of inferior produce. What I propose to discuss is not the fact itself, the reasons for which are obvious, but the enigmatic mechanism whereby music, that has once been famous and appreciated, may disappear, temporarily or completely, and mus
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 i\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 c which has for one reason or another remained}{\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  unrecognised}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  may be revived.
\par }\pard \qj \fi306\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx306\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15491189 {\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
At a time when publication was rare, musicians had a realistic attitude to the problem:}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 they wrote their music for an actual demand or occasion and nobody thought about its durabil\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 ity. It may even have contributed to the artist\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s integrity that he was undisturbed by ambition, that he had no other thought on his mind than to fulfil honestly a task of the moment. This was Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s attitude and this was Haydn\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s when the one had to write\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 a church cantata for the following Sunday, or the other a symphony for his princely employer\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s next dinner party. They did their best as honest craftsmen.
\par }\pard \qj \fi306\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx306\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
Well, contemporaries did not always recognise the great musician amongst a crowd of inferiors, and hi\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 s situation was particularly problematic when his music had only the scantiest chance of becoming known. When Bach, in 1723}{
\b\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 , }{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
took charge of church music in Leipzig, Germany was still suffering from the ravages of the Thirty Years War and a musician's activ\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
ity was restricted within the narrowest limits. The tiny fraction of his works that Bach was able to publish, at his own expense, hardly gave him any publicity. When he died in 1750}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid15491189 
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 ,}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  none but a handful of friends and disciples bothered about his music. Nev\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
ertheless, it survived at St Thomas\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s Cathedral, where Mozart heard a motet of his when he passed through Leipzig in 1789. Several years before he had had a chance to lay hands on a handwritten copy of the \hich\f0 \lquote 
\loch\f0 Forty-Eight\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 , and the impression it made on him \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 w\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 as decisive for the later developme}{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 nt}
{\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  of his style. Thus Mozart became the first posthumous disciple of Bach. Beethoven, a pupil of Neefe, who had been a pupil of Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s son Carl Philip Emanuel, already grew up with the \hich\f0 \lquote \loch\f0 Forty-Eight\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0  and he studied them al\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 l his life.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 I mention this in order to emphasise how problematic the chance of survival of great music still was in the eighteenth century. Handel, Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s close contemporary, was fortunate; he lived in a wealthy country and enjoyed the patronage of a rich \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 aristocracy. Handel\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s and Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s positions in the world were as different as a palace and a hovel. This is why Bach's work offers the most spectacular example of buried treasure and its exhumation. Mendelssohn's performance of the St Matthew Passion in Be\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 r
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 lin in 1829, a century after the first performance in Leipzig, paved the way for further progress in the recovery of Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s music. But only in 1850, at the centenary of Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s death, was a complete edition of his works started, the last volume of which di\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 d\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  not appear until the end of the century. Bach\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s posthumous influence was enormous and there was no musician of the nineteenth century who escaped it, perhaps with the sole exception of Berlioz. For Brahms the annual volume of the Bach Complete Edition to\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 which he had subscribed meant more than any contemporary score that ever came into his hands.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Nor was Bach the only great composer of his time who had to be discovered by posterity. Another close contemporary of his, Domenico Scarlatti, who lived at the Sp\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
anish court in Madrid, was almost equally secluded from publicity. His sonatas for harpsichord, one}{\b\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  }{
\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 of the most magnificent contributions to keyboard music of all times, had to wait until our century to become accessible in a complete edition.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 Dictionaries\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
