\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
an composers was maintained in the operatic repertory was hardly the result of such highbrow criticism but rather of a natural selection from an enormous supply. Here we are confronted with the phenomenon of total or temporary disfavour into which works c
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 a\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 n fall which, once upon a time, were favourites. And the occasional rediscovery of such forgotten works\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 we have witnessed a great many of Rossini\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s, Donizetti\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s, Bellini\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s and Verdi\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 s operas revived after many years\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 is equally puzzling. Apart from a chang\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 e
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
 of fashion which may cause a temporary or definite eclipse, and intrinsic qualities which are certainly the most decisive justification of a rediscovery, our century has developed an inexhaustible curiosity for the creative output of previous periods and
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
centuries, and the results are sometimes questionable. The great cemetery of forgotten music, opened to the diggers, has been turned over and over at an ever increasing speed since the complete editions of the works of the great classics inaugurated a per
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 i\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 od of unlimited historical interest.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 It is a tricky specialist\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s job to arrive at an authentic, reliable text from sometimes contradictory manuscript sources, and it may happen that the enthusiasm of a discovery may prevail over a critical appreciation of \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 the object\hich\f0 \rquote 
\loch\f0 s artistic value. I have before me the score of an opera by Gluck, }{\i\lang1033\langfe2052\langnp1033\insrsid2688811\charrsid15491189 \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 L\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 Innocen}{
